# Code owners for SUM Chain.
#
# SCOPED DELIBERATELY (#219). This file is NOT a whole-tree owner list: it names
# owners only for the GOVERNANCE paths, so that "Require review from Code Owners"
# can be enabled WITHOUT forcing a human approval on every ordinary PR.
#
# Why this exists: the automated-review gate (docs/governance/AUTOMATED-REVIEW.md)
# replaces the human-approval count for ordinary PRs, but its clause 4 cannot
# catch a PR that rewrites the gate WORKFLOW itself to trivially pass. The
# intended compensating control was a ruleset "Restrict file paths" rule; GitHub
# rejects that rule on this org's plan (422, Enterprise-gated). CODEOWNERS +
# "Require review from Code Owners" gives the same guarantee on any plan:
# a PR touching these paths requires a code-owner approval; every other PR
# requires none.
#
# TWO owners are named on purpose. A single-owner entry would deadlock the
# owner's own governance PRs (an author cannot approve their own PR) — the exact
# reason whole-tree code-owner review was previously left OFF.
#
# Keep this in sync with `gate_paths` in .github/automated-review.config.json.

